[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-72465"] :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(B)=-2.$ What is the value of $det(3B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot B)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=3$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(3B) & ={3}^{2}\\cdot det(B) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-130739/selection/ae1ec0bcc83ac82fe7d363f2ad54fe23dc343f2913e126433b39173ac74d85e6" :answer/id #uuid "8b2f192f-2748-5265-96d7-cd12fd7aacfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "160" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130739/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer/id #uuid "b2da7c29-cefe-5090-81c6-f5dd571a32f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130739/selection/9a2c0f137f7fb9298cf3554da60658106395d030c4c60175330a7e0c456976f5" :answer/id #uuid "b45bae58-9882-59d5-9b7a-c988374c5c88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130739/selection/1bca1d8d2aa1971b466bdadf96ec22a648cbfa817c046e8034441b24ba905593" :answer/id #uuid "9708b244-f64c-5021-bea5-de40ca1711ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-88" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130739/selection/34ca4becb78d2c61c238ca94df2147379242ec948066b96abbc029ecbfe2beb0" :answer/id #uuid "32452624-c669-5a2a-af81-9a45d8922ef4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-128" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130739/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0886aaa0-7d4a-5c70-b7ea-32b77b2b39a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130739/selection/34ca4becb78d2c61c238ca94df2147379242ec948066b96abbc029ecbfe2beb0" :answer-field/choices ["q-130739/selection/ae1ec0bcc83ac82fe7d363f2ad54fe23dc343f2913e126433b39173ac74d85e6" "q-130739/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" "q-130739/selection/9a2c0f137f7fb9298cf3554da60658106395d030c4c60175330a7e0c456976f5" "q-130739/selection/1bca1d8d2aa1971b466bdadf96ec22a648cbfa817c046e8034441b24ba905593" "q-130739/selection/34ca4becb78d2c61c238ca94df2147379242ec948066b96abbc029ecbfe2beb0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130739" :question/id #uuid "8b833eb4-9e05-5944-8297-af141a86129b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130739" :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(Y)=2.$ What is the value of $det(-4Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-4$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-4Y) & =(-4)^{3}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =-64\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-128.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130739/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "272d9a54-ba97-5175-86df-0a78337da7b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130739"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130771/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" :answer/id #uuid "f268ffaf-758c-541d-a3af-ed74bd78a24e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130771/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer/id #uuid "e3f7ce9a-2702-5c4a-adc7-2cb51679018c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130771/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "7f2324e3-8eea-513b-84cb-8b138002693e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130771/selection/74dee60e2d310a70b6506a0bbb9d1a5efe998972e06348f66a7e85d3fd6c23dd" :answer/id #uuid "afb71e20-5159-5ba5-aaff-5a081cb43436" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130771/selection/f4ed4b34f4a5de49898377314514d2de061007c11b4d8d545eea74864f386ee8" :answer/id #uuid "fe8d28ab-d8e0-54f1-ae2f-41748d5803c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130771/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef923b97-f042-51db-894b-b3bdccf2e667" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130771/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-130771/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" "q-130771/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" "q-130771/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" "q-130771/selection/74dee60e2d310a70b6506a0bbb9d1a5efe998972e06348f66a7e85d3fd6c23dd" "q-130771/selection/f4ed4b34f4a5de49898377314514d2de061007c11b4d8d545eea74864f386ee8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130771" :question/id #uuid "f84f51ef-7655-5ddd-814b-3221e5dd4c7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130771" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=-75.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{6}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{4}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $\\frac{4}{5},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot (-75) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130771/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24e5e193-5e30-5480-9e5d-b7b8f1d5de87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130771"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130855/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "86d825ee-7b34-5102-97b3-21279d710693" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130855/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "6f145981-0fb0-583c-b651-8f4a66d6d2e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130855/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "3e5a599c-e48f-5169-b52c-171486d54184" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130855/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "efd1fd85-dcdb-5304-86df-874588915e6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130855/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "b5d27282-1505-5bc2-ba89-acb51d1328ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130855/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca72fa80-1e05-538a-bf3b-8898e7d8d5ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130855/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-130855/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-130855/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" "q-130855/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-130855/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-130855/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130855" :question/id #uuid "2147c852-ca7d-56cf-bfc5-b94dd52d4711" :question/math-academy-id "q-130855" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=5$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(5) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130855/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130855"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130857/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "bc4b19f5-5156-5af2-86ba-7ecd0757ea0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130857/selection/4fa830bda994f89067ddecaf273e4fa78aa4d8447b6388b70cafa0fc166e6f67" :answer/id #uuid "afb16502-e271-5984-9