ion "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $1$st and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(-60) \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130857/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130857"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
